/**
 * Every tunable modelling assumption the simulator makes, gathered in one inspectable place and
 * carried on {@link SimScenario#assumptions} / {@link SimulationInput#assumptions}.
 *
 * This type exists so that mock values are **not scattered through the engine or the UI**. If a
 * number is a guess, it belongs here, where the review interface can display it and a reviewer
 * can see what the result depends on. None of these defaults are agreed operational facts about
 * MTD.
 *
 * All durations are in **minutes** unless the field name says seconds.
 */
type SimAssumptions {

  /**
   * Dwell time, in minutes, used for a supplemental-trip stop call when boarding/alighting time
   * does not already exceed it. The effective dwell is
   * `max(defaultDwellMinutes, passengers * per-passenger seconds / 60)`.
   */
  defaultDwellMinutes: double

  /** Seconds of dwell added per boarding passenger, converted to minutes by the engine. */
  boardingSecondsPerPassenger: double

  /** Seconds of dwell added per alighting passenger. */
  alightingSecondsPerPassenger: double

  /**
   * How {@link SimEvent#confidence} and {@link SimReputationScore#reliability} are turned into the
   * weight multiplying expected demand:
   * - `None` — weight is always 1.0; confidence is recorded but ignored.
   * - `ConfidenceOnly` — weight = confidence.
   * - `ReputationOnly` — weight = reputation of the reporting user / the event.
   * - `ConfidenceTimesReputation` — weight = confidence * reputation.
   *
   * The last option multiplies two measures that may not be independent; it is offered because
   * it is the intuitive default, but the product is **not** a calibrated probability and
   * {@link SimReconciliationEntry#rationale} records the assumption explicitly for every event it
   * is applied to. Scheduled events are exempt: a timetabled class is not discounted.
   */
  reliabilityPolicy: !string enum('None','ConfidenceOnly','ReputationOnly','ConfidenceTimesReputation')

  /**
   * Weight substituted for a missing {@link SimEvent#confidence}, on 0..1. Deliberately below 1.0
   * so that an estimate arriving with no stated confidence is not treated as certain.
   */
  defaultConfidence: double

  /**
   * Weight substituted for a missing {@link SimReputationScore}, on 0..1. A neutral value (0.5 in
   * the mock scenarios) — an unknown reporter is neither trusted nor dismissed.
   */
  defaultReputation: double

  /**
   * Ceiling applied to the combined travel-time multiplier on any link, after
   * {@link SimAssumptions#overlappingMultiplierRule} has combined overlapping effects.
   *
   * Prevents a stack of coincident disruptions from producing an absurd travel time. When the
   * clamp binds, {@link SimResolvedEffects#clampApplied} is set so the result is not silently
   * misleading.
   */
  maxTravelTimeMultiplier: double

  /**
   * How two or more `TravelTimeMultiplier` effects active on the **same** link at the **same**
   * time combine:
   * - `Multiply` — multipliers compound (1.5 and 1.4 give 2.1). Treats disruptions as independent
   *   causes of delay; the default.
   * - `Max` — the worst single multiplier wins (1.5 and 1.4 give 1.5). Appropriate if overlapping
   *   reports are suspected to describe the same congestion.
   * Either way the result is clamped to {@link SimAssumptions#maxTravelTimeMultiplier} and retains
   * {@link SimEffectInterval#sourceEventIds}.
   */
  overlappingMultiplierRule: !string enum('Multiply','Max')

  /**
   * Which producer wins when a {@link SimStudentLocationEstimate} and a {@link SimEvent} describe
   * the same population — detected by {@link SimStudentLocationEstimate#linkedEventId}, or by a
   * shared {@link SimDemandEffect#cohortId}.
   *
   * `PreferEvent` keeps the event's demand effect and suppresses the estimate;
   * `PreferLocationEstimate` does the reverse. Exactly one side generates passengers, so a cohort
   * can never appear twice merely because two producers mentioned it. The decision is recorded as
   * a `CohortOverlapResolved` {@link SimReconciliationEntry}.
   */
  cohortOverlapPolicy: !string enum('PreferEvent','PreferLocationEstimate')

  /**
   * Half-width, in minutes, of the time tolerance used by the fallback matcher that pairs a
   * {@link SimEventReport} with a canonical {@link SimEvent} when the report carries no event
   * reference. A report must also name a stop listed in {@link SimEvent#affectedStopIds}.
   *
   * Fallback matching is a documented mock heuristic. Real producers are expected to share
   * canonical event ids instead.
   */
  reportMatchWindowMinutes: int

  /**
   * Whether passengers may change buses. **False** in this implementation: every generated
   * journey is a direct origin-to-destination trip, and a passenger is never boarded onto a trip
   * that cannot reach their destination.
   *
   * Recorded as a field rather than hard-coded so the limitation is visible in exports. Setting it
   * true is not yet supported and is rejected by {@link SimInputAssembler#validate}.
   */
  allowTransfers: boolean

  /**
   * Queue discipline at a stop. `FifoByRequestTime`: among passengers eligible for a given
   * vehicle, the one who arrived at the stop earliest boards first, ties broken by the stable
   * journey id so the result is fully deterministic.
   *
   * Eligibility is destination-aware, so FIFO applies *within* the set of passengers the vehicle
   * can actually serve; a passenger at the head of the queue whose destination is not on the trip
   * does not block the queue behind them.
   */
  queueDiscipline: !string enum('FifoByRequestTime')

  /**
   * How an arrival **window** becomes individual arrival instants:
   * - `UniformDeterministic` — passengers are spread evenly across the window at fixed
   *   fractions, independent of the seed. Fully reproducible and the easier behaviour to reason
   *   about in tests.
   * - `SeededUniform` — arrival instants are drawn from the seeded PRNG, giving a more realistic
   *   clumpy arrival pattern that is still reproducible for a given
   *   {@link SimScenario#randomSeed}.
   */
  arrivalWindowDistribution: !string enum('UniformDeterministic','SeededUniform')

  /**
   * Width, in minutes, of the time buckets used to report expected wait by stop in
   * {@link SimResults#stopWindowDelays} and in the student-facing delay export. 15 or 30 minutes
   * in the mock scenarios.
   */
  stopDelayWindowMinutes: int

  /**
   * Average speed, in km/h, assumed when a bus must reposition between two stops that have no
   * explicit {@link SimTravelLink}. Combined with the great-circle distance between the stops'
   * coordinates to estimate deadhead minutes.
   *
   * A deliberately crude fallback; it keeps the planner from assuming instantaneous
   * repositioning, which would be the far worse error.
   */
  deadheadSpeedKmPerHour: double

  /**
   * Minimum idle minutes required between one trip's last arrival and the same bus's next
   * departure. Guarantees itineraries that are physically runnable and, with the travel-time
   * check, is what makes overlapping trips for a single bus impossible.
   */
  minTurnaroundMinutes: double
}
